e have all and we are all making  choices and we're doing it together and  that is a really critical critical  aspect of this um i don't quite know how  this will resolve but i think that the  emphasis that i will put here  is on the partnership that we see  between the u.s the uk the europeans  other allies in taking joint action  and really standing up for a system of  values and principles that is important  to our vision of a better world  and just bringing things back to the uk  u.s relationship  what are the key things that you'd like  to see from british business and the  british government that would speed up  the process of  some form of a free trade deal well uh  let me put it this way what i have seen  from  the british government and the british  people is also a shared set of  priorities and values around the need  for resilience for sustainability in  terms of our economic relations and  ensuring that our economic and trade  system  is incentivizing  behavior that puts the interests of our  people and our planet first because  without that  uh we're all in very deep trouble and  and a free trade deal is what a year  away or or many many years away again  we will see what form our collaboration  takes but regardless of the form  i think that there is a lot that we have  to accomplish together
 

